          "secNumber": "3.11",
          "heading": "Unit 3 Methodological Synthesis and Review",
          "content": "Measurement theory provides the rigorous quantitative bridge between unobservable scientific constructs and empirical manifest data:\n- Match statistical analysis procedures strictly to the Stevens scale level of measurement (nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio).\n- Understand the foundational decomposition of Classical Test Theory ($\\sigma_X^2 = \\sigma_T^2 + \\sigma_E^2$) and recognize that random measurement error severely attenuates observed correlations.\n- Move beyond the limitations of Cronbach's alpha by verifying essential $\\tau$-equivalence, reporting McDonald's $\\omega_{\\text{total}}$, and evaluating dimensionality via factor analysis.\n- Deploy the Campbell-Fiske MTMM matrix to decouple substantive construct variance from common method variance.\n- Leverage modern Item Response Theory (1PL, 2PL, 3PL) and information functions to optimize measurement precision across the trait continuum and verify measurement invariance across demographic groups.",
