              "explanation": "We wish to increase reliability from the current baseline $\\rho_{11} = 0.840$ to $\\rho_{kk} = 0.90$.\nThe general Spearman-Brown formula is:\n$$\\rho_{kk} = \\frac{k \\rho_{11}}{1 + (k - 1)\\rho_{11}}$$\nSolve algebraically for the lengthening multiplier $k$:\n$$\\rho_{kk} [1 + (k - 1)\\rho_{11}] = k \\rho_{11}$$\n$$\\rho_{kk} + k \\rho_{kk} \\rho_{11} - \\rho_{kk} \\rho_{11} = k \\rho_{11}$$\n$$\\rho_{kk} (1 - \\rho_{11}) = k \\rho_{11} (1 - \\rho_{kk})$$\n$$k = \\frac{\\rho_{kk} (1 - \\rho_{11})}{\\rho_{11} (1 - \\rho_{kk})}$$\nSubstitute $\\rho_{11} = 0.840$ and target $\\rho_{kk} = 0.90$:\n$$k = \\frac{0.90 \\times (1 - 0.840)}{0.840 \\times (1 - 0.90)} = \\frac{0.90 \\times 0.160}{0.840 \\times 0.10} = \\frac{0.144}{0.084} \\approx 1.7143$$\nThe test must be lengthened by a factor of $1.7143$.\nThe total number of required items is:\n$$N_{\\text{items}} = 6 \\times 1.7143 = 10.286 \\implies \\mathbf{11 \\text{ items}}$$\nThe test developers must add $11 - 6 = \\mathbf{5 \\text{ additional parallel items}}$ to achieve a reliability exceeding $0.90$."
